<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane Fifi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Hurricane Fifi–Orlene</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane Fifi was a tropical cyclone that skirted the north coast of Honduras in September 1974, bringing torrential rain that caused catastrophic flooding and landslides. It killed an estimated 3,000 to 10,000 people, most of them in Honduras, and destroyed much of the banana crop and the country's infrastructure, making it one of the deadliest Atlantic hurricanes of the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-fifi.jpg" alt="Hurricane Fifi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NOAA (SMS-1), SSEC/CIMSS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fifi_1974-09-18_2130Z_color.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
